ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 784871, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01MwG1QV8cStkG97pLYfkQJC", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 785171, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01MwG1QV8cStkG97pLYfkQJC", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 785171, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01MwG1QV8cStkG97pLYfkQJC", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 787221, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "The problem was in `payments-worker`, not `payments-api`. It's rolled back and healthy again, and the SEV2 incident is open.\n\n- **Rollback:** `payments-worker` went from v3.4.0 to v3.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Its error rate is now 0.2%, down from 18%, and it reports healthy.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001, SEV2, against `payments-worker`. It summarizes the v3.4.0 errors and the rollback, and it paged on-call.\n\nI first rolled back `payments-api` from v5.1.0 to v5.0.0 and opened an incident for it. A human approver denied both actions, saying the problem was in `payments-worker`. Those denials mean nothing was changed on `payments-api`, so it's still on v5.1.0 with an 18% error rate. Someone should confirm whether it's affected too.\n\nThe v3.4.0 root cause still needs investigating before it's redeployed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01WQFfP49RsNULw1SEN9KNMg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01ABRvj